<title>USA: Sacramento, Calif., furloughs workers for a day.</title>
<headline>Sacramento, Calif., furloughs workers for a day.</headline>
<dateline>SACRAMENTO, Calif. 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Most Sacramento County government offices were closed Friday for the cash-strapped county's first mandatory furlough day, according to a published report.</p>
<p>About 7,500 of the county's 10,400 employees were told to take the day off without pay, forcing the closure of most county departments, the Sacramento Bee newspaper reported.</p>
<p>County supervisors last year approved three furlough days for most employees to balance the county's budget. The cost-cutting move was expected to save $500,000 for each furlough day. The other furlough dates are May 23 and June 13.</p>
</text>
